      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;the-problem&#34;&gt;The problem&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Given an array of integers &lt;code&gt;heights&lt;/code&gt; representing the histogram&amp;rsquo;s bar height where the width of each bar is &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, return the area of the largest rectangle in the histogram.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;examples&#34;&gt;Examples&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; id=&#34;zoomCheck-f3e90&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;    &lt;label for=&#34;zoomCheck-f3e90&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img class=&#34;zoomCheck&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; decoding=&#34;async&#34; &#xA;            src=&#34;images/histogram.jpg#center&#34; alt=&#34;alt image&#34; &#xA;             /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/label&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Input: heights = [2,1,5,6,2,3]  &#xA;Output: 10  &#xA;Explanation: The above is a histogram where width of each bar is 1.  &#xA;The largest rectangle is shown in the red area, which has an area = 10 units.  &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; id=&#34;zoomCheck-1deaf&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;    &lt;label for=&#34;zoomCheck-1deaf&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img class=&#34;zoomCheck&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; decoding=&#34;async&#34; &#xA;            src=&#34;images/histogram-1.jpg#center&#34; alt=&#34;alt image&#34; &#xA;             /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/label&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
